76,"seed":379236248110102185,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the polynomial \\(4x^4 - ax^3 + bx^2 - cx + 5\\) with roots \\(r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4\\), we apply Vieta's formulas to relate the coefficients to the roots. Specifically, Vieta's formulas give us:\n\\[\nr_1 + r_2 + r_3 + r_4 = \\frac{a}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\nr_1r_2 + r_1r_3 + r_1r_4 + r_2r_3 + r_2r_4 + r_3r_4 = \\frac{b}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\nr_1r_2r_3 + r_1r_2r_4 + r_1r_3r_4 + r_2r_3r_4 = \\frac{c}{4}\n\\]\n\\[\nr_1r_2r_3r_4 = \\frac{5}{4}\n\\]\n\nAdditionally, we are given the condition:\n\\[\n\\frac{r_1}{2} + \\frac{r_2}{4} + \\frac{r_3}{5} + \\frac{r_4}{8} = 1\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(a\\), we first need to express \\(a\\) in terms of the roots. From Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[\na = 4(r_1 + r_2 + r_3 + r_4)\n\\]\n\nNext, we introduce a substitution to simplify the given condition. Let:\n\\[\nr_1 = 2x, \\quad r_2 = 4y, \\quad r_3 = 5z, \\quad r_4 = 8w\n\\]\nThen the given condition becomes:\n\\[\nx + y + z + w = 1\n\\]\n\nThe product of the roots is:\n\\[\nr_1r_2r_3r_4 = (2x)(4y)(5z)(8w) = 320xyzw = \\frac{5}{4}\n\\]\nThus,\n\\[\n320xyzw = \\frac{5}{4} \\implies xyzw = \\frac{5}{1280} = \\frac{1}{256}\n\\]\n\nNow we need to find \\(r_1 + r_2 + r_3 + r_4\\):\n\\[\nr_1 + r_2 + r_3 + r_4 = 2x + 4y + 5z + 8w\n\\]\n\nTo find the sum \\(2x + 4y + 5z + 8w\\), we use the method of Lagrange multipliers or symmetry arguments. Since \\(x + y + z + w = 1\\) and \\(xyzw = \\frac{1}{256}\\), we can assume \\(x = y = z = w = \\frac{1}{4}\\) by symmetry (since the product is a constant and the sum is a constant, the simplest symmetric solution is equal parts).\n\nThus,\n\\[\n2x + 4y + 5z + 8w = 2\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) + 5\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) + 8\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = \\frac{2}{4} + \\frac{4}{4} + \\frac{5}{4} + \\frac{8}{4} = \\frac{19}{4}\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\\[\na = 4 \\left(\\frac{19}{4}\\right) = 19\n\\]\n\nThe value of \\(a\\) is \\(\\boxed{19}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{19}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
